# C3 Hays website — environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local dev, or set these in your host
# (Vercel / GitHub Actions). The site has TWO deploy targets that coexist:
#
#   1. Static export  → GitHub Pages (default; CMS_LIVE unset). Hand-built pages.
#   2. Live SSR        → Vercel (CMS_LIVE=1). Server-renders from C3 Studio.
#
# Nothing here is secret — these are public configuration toggles.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_URL — base URL of the C3 Studio (CMS) content API.
#   Unset (default)  → CMS calls short-circuit to null; site renders its
#                       hand-built static pages (GitHub Pages path).
#   Set              → pages fetch PUBLISHED content from C3 Studio's
#                       /api/content endpoints.
#   Production:  https://studio.c3hays.com
#   Local dev:   http://localhost:4544
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_URL=https://studio.c3hays.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMS_LIVE — selects the build/runtime mode (see next.config.ts).
#   unset / not "1" → output: "export" (static, GitHub Pages). DEFAULT.
#   1               → output: undefined (server runtime / SSR for Vercel).
#                     Required for live, real-time CMS rendering — a build-time
#                     static export cannot fetch live content per request.
# Set CMS_LIVE=1 together with NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_URL for the live production path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMS_LIVE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH — sub-path prefix. GITHUB PAGES ONLY.
#   GitHub Pages serves project sites at /<repo-name>/, so the Pages CI build
#   sets this to /c3hays-redesign (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
#   Leave UNSET for local dev, for a custom apex domain (c3hays.com), and for
#   the Vercel SSR deploy (served at the domain root).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/c3hays-redesign
